astle (which can be entered to the south) and the moat. A young elm grows by the side of the moat. A causeway leads out into the moat to the northwest. Entrance Hall A proclamation hangs on the wall. Entrance Hall This is where visitors enter the castle proper, through the wide doorway to the north. Oddly, there is a doorbell on the inside of the doorway. Other doorways lead east, west, and south. A proclamation hangs on the wall. Banquet Hall You can see a cauldron here. Banquet Hall Many royal feasts have been held in this hall, which could easily hold ten thousand guests. Legends say that Dimwit's more excessive banquets would require the combined farm outputs of three provinces. The primary exits are to the west and south; smaller openings lead east and northeast. You can see a cauldron here. With a puff of magically charged smoke, the T-square vanishes amidst the vapors. The cauldron's level of activity seems to increase. [Your score has just gone up by 5.] With a puff of magically charged smoke, the fancy violin vanishes amidst the vapors. The cauldron's level of activity seems to increase; it is now bubbling actively. [Your score has just gone up by 5.] Courtyard This open area is paved with marble and surrounded by imposing stone walls. Dimwit would occasionally order carnivals to be set up in this court, on totally cloudless days. At the distant edges of the courtyard, you can see exits to the north, west, and southeast. Courtyard This open area is paved with marble and surrounded by imposing stone walls. Dimwit would occasionally order carnivals to be set up in this court, on totally cloudless days. At the distant edges of the courtyard, you can see exits to the north, west, and southeast. East Hall The castle's east wing lies through a massive door to the east, which is closed. The only other exit from the hall is northwest. East Hall The castle's east wing lies through a massive door to the east, which is closed. The only other exit from the hall is nort